#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:121
msgid "`===` vs `==`"
msgstr "`===` срещу `==`"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:123
msgid "MDN: [Strict equality (===)](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/Strict_equality), [Equality (==)](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/Equality)"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:125
msgid "`==` first **converts** the two values to the same type, then compares. The conversion rules are long and surprising:"
msgstr "`==` първо **преобразува** двете стойности до един и същ тип и след това ги сравнява. Правилата за преобразуване са дълги и изненадващи:"

#. box title
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:138
msgid "Use `===` and `!==`"
msgstr "Използвайте `===` и `!==`"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:139
msgid "They never convert. What you see is what is compared. All comparisons in the course use `===` / `!==`. The one `==` worth knowing is below."
msgstr "Те никога не преобразуват. Сравнява се точно това, което виждате. Всички сравнения в курса използват `===` / `!==`. Единственото `==`, което си струва да знаете, е по-долу."

#. box title
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:143 site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:246 site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:395 site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:512 site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:643 site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:816 site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:860 site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:896 site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:959 site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1049 site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1130 site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1158 site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1208
msgid "Animation"
msgstr "Анимация"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:144
msgid "**Types, comparisons and logic:** [3. `==` and `===`](../animations/coercionAndLogic.html#3){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Типове, сравнения и логика:** [3. `==` и `===`](../animations/coercionAndLogic.html#3){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:147
msgid "The one useful `==`: `null` and `undefined`"
msgstr "Единственото полезно `==`: `null` и `undefined`"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:149
msgid "`null == undefined` is `true`, and `null` / `undefined` are not loosely equal to anything else. So `value == null` means \"`value` is `null` **or** `undefined`\":"
msgstr "`null == undefined` е `true`, а `null` / `undefined` не са нестрого равни на нищо друго. Затова `value == null` означава \"`value` е `null` **или** `undefined`\":"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:161
msgid "You will see both forms in existing rules, and both are correct. In new code, choose one form and use it everywhere."
msgstr "В съществуващите правила ще видите и двете форми, и двете са правилни. В нов код изберете едната форма и я използвайте навсякъде."

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:164
msgid "`NaN` is not equal to anything"
msgstr "`NaN` не е равно на нищо"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:173
msgid "Comparing decimals"
msgstr "Сравняване на дробни числа"

#. box title
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:181
msgid "Objects are compared by reference"
msgstr "Обектите се сравняват по референция"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:182
msgid "`{} === {}` and `[] === []` are `false`: two objects are equal only if they are **the same object**. More in session 6."
msgstr "`{} === {}` и `[] === []` са `false`: два обекта са равни само ако са **един и същ обект**. Повече в занятие 6."

#. box title
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:186
msgid "Animations"
msgstr "Анимации"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:187
msgid "**Numbers in memory:** [4. 0.1 + 0.2](../animations/numbersInMemory.html#4){target=\"_blank\"}, [6. NaN and Infinity](../animations/numbersInMemory.html#6){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Числата в паметта:** [4. 0.1 + 0.2](../animations/numbersInMemory.html#4){target=\"_blank\"}, [6. NaN и Infinity](../animations/numbersInMemory.html#6){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 2
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:190
msgid "2. Comparing strings"
msgstr "2. Сравняване на strings"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:192
msgid "Two strings are compared **character by character**, by the character codes (Unicode). This is called *lexicographic* order - like in a dictionary:"
msgstr "Два strings се сравняват **символ по символ**, по кодовете на символите (Unicode). Това се нарича *лексикографски* ред - като в речник:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:205
msgid "If one string is a prefix of the other, the shorter one is smaller."
msgstr "Ако единият string е начало на другия, по-късият е по-малък."

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:207
msgid "Why `\"4.10\" < \"4.2\"` is `true`"
msgstr "Защо `\"4.10\" < \"4.2\"` е `true`"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:209
msgid "Versions are strings. Compared as strings, they give **wrong** answers:"
msgstr "Версиите са strings. Сравнени като strings, те дават **грешни** отговори:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:217
msgid "A version must be compared **part by part, as numbers**: 4 = 4, then 10 > 2. We write such a helper, `versionBelow(a, b)`, in session 5. Until then the practice tasks give it to you ready-made."
msgstr "Версията трябва да се сравнява **част по част, като числа**: 4 = 4, после 10 > 2. Такава helper функция, `versionBelow(a, b)`, ще напишем в занятие 5. Дотогава задачите за упражнение ви я дават готова."

#. box title
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:221
msgid "Mixed types"
msgstr "Смесени типове"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:222
msgid "When one side is a number, the string is converted to a number: `\"10\" > 9` is `true`, but `\"10\" > \"9\"` is `false`. And `\"abc\" < 5` and `\"abc\" >= 5` are both `false` (`NaN`). Convert first, then compare."
msgstr "Когато едната страна е number, string-ът се преобразува в number: `\"10\" > 9` е `true`, но `\"10\" > \"9\"` е `false`. А `\"abc\" < 5` и `\"abc\" >= 5` са `false` и двете (`NaN`). Първо преобразувайте, после сравнявайте."

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:227
msgid "Upper and lower case"
msgstr "Главни и малки букви"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:229
msgid "`===` is case-sensitive. JSON values are not always written the same way, so compare in one case. `toLowerCase()` gives the same text in lower case (more string methods in session 8):"
msgstr "`===` различава малки и главни букви. Стойностите в JSON не винаги са написани по един и същ начин, затова сравнявайте в един регистър. `toLowerCase()` дава същия текст с малки букви (повече методи на strings в занятие 8):"

#. box title
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:239
msgid "Natural order (preview)"
msgstr "Естествен ред (поглед напред)"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:240
msgid "`\"4.10\".localeCompare(\"4.2\", undefined, { numeric: true })` gives `1` (bigger), because it reads digit groups as numbers. Useful for sorting (session 7), but our version formats vary too much (`4.2.1.7-B00`, `42107-C00`), so for rules we write our own comparison."
msgstr "`\"4.10\".localeCompare(\"4.2\", undefined, { numeric: true })` дава `1` (по-голямо), защото чете групите от цифри като числа. Полезно е за сортиране (занятие 7), но нашите формати на версиите са твърде различни (`4.2.1.7-B00`, `42107-C00`), затова за правилата пишем собствено сравнение."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:247
msgid "**Types, comparisons and logic:** [4. Comparing strings](../animations/coercionAndLogic.html#4){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Типове, сравнения и логика:** [4. Сравняване на strings](../animations/coercionAndLogic.html#4){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 2
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:250
msgid "3. Logical operators"
msgstr "3. Логически оператори"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:252
msgid "MDN: [Logical AND (&&)](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/Logical_AND), [Logical OR (||)](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/Logical_OR), [Logical NOT (!)](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/Logical_NOT)"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:254
msgid "Logical operators combine conditions:"
msgstr "Логическите оператори комбинират условия:"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:256
msgid "Name"
msgstr "Име"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:256
msgid "`true` when"
msgstr "`true`, когато"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:258
msgid "AND"
msgstr "И (AND)"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:258
msgid "both are true"
msgstr "и двете са истина"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:259
msgid "OR"
msgstr "ИЛИ (OR)"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:259
msgid "at least one is true"
msgstr "поне едното е истина"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:260
msgid "NOT"
msgstr "НЕ (NOT)"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:260
msgid "`a` is false"
msgstr "`a` е неистина"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:262
msgid "The truth table (T - true, F - false):"
msgstr "Таблицата на истинност (T - true, F - false):"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:271
msgid "`&&` and `||` take two operands; `!` takes one (it is *unary*)."
msgstr "`&&` и `||` имат два операнда; `!` има един (той е *унарен*)."

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:291
msgid "Precedence and parentheses"
msgstr "Приоритет и скоби"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:293
msgid "MDN: [Operator precedence](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/Operator_precedence)"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:295
msgid "`!` is applied first, then `&&`, then `||` - like `*` before `+`:"
msgstr "Първо се прилага `!`, после `&&`, после `||` - както `*` преди `+`:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:303
msgid "When a condition mixes `&&` and `||`, **always** add parentheses - for the reader, not only for JavaScript:"
msgstr "Когато едно условие смесва `&&` и `||`, **винаги** слагайте скоби - заради читателя, не само заради JavaScript:"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:310
msgid "Turning a condition around (De Morgan)"
msgstr "Обръщане на условие (De Morgan)"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:312
msgid "To write \"**not** (A and B)\", flip each part and change `&&` to `||`:"
msgstr "За да напишете \"**не** (A и B)\", обърнете всяка част и сменете `&&` с `||`:"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:314
msgid "This"
msgstr "Това"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:314
msgid "is the same as"
msgstr "е същото като"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:319
msgid "You need this for guard clauses (section 6): \"stop if the model is neither XR-210 nor XR-220\" is `if (model !== \"XR-210\" && model !== \"XR-220\") return;`."
msgstr "Това ви трябва за guard clauses (раздел 6): \"спри, ако моделът не е нито XR-210, нито XR-220\" е `if (model !== \"XR-210\" && model !== \"XR-220\") return;`."

#. heading 2
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:322
msgid "4. Truthy and falsy"
msgstr "4. Truthy и falsy"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:324
msgid "MDN: [Truthy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Truthy), [Falsy](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Falsy)"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:326
msgid "`if (...)`, `!`, `&&` and `||` accept **any** value, not only booleans. The value is then treated as `true` or `false`. These eight values are **falsy**:"
msgstr "`if (...)`, `!`, `&&` и `||` приемат **всякаква** стойност, не само booleans. Тогава стойността се третира като `true` или `false`. Тези осем стойности са **falsy**:"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:329
msgid "Type"
msgstr "Тип"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:329
msgid "Falsy values"
msgstr "Falsy стойности"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:331
msgid "boolean"
msgstr "boolean"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:332
msgid "number"
msgstr "number"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:332
msgid "`0`, `-0`, `NaN` (and `0n`, a bigint)"
msgstr "`0`, `-0`, `NaN` (и `0n`, който е bigint)"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:333
msgid "string"
msgstr "string"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:333
msgid "`\"\"` (the empty string)"
msgstr "`\"\"` (празният string)"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:336
msgid "**Everything else is truthy** - including `\"0\"`, `\"false\"`, `\"no\"`, `\" \"`, `[]` and `{}`."
msgstr "**Всичко останало е truthy** - включително `\"0\"`, `\"false\"`, `\"no\"`, `\" \"`, `[]` и `{}`."

#. box title
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:349
msgid "`\"no\"` is truthy"
msgstr "`\"no\"` е truthy"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:350
msgid "The report stores yes / no settings as text: `\"remote_login_enabled\": \"yes\"`, `\"remote_login_pwd_set\": \"no\"`. `if (doc.inventory.details.remote_login_pwd_set)` is true for `\"no\"` too - every non-empty string is truthy. Compare with the value you mean: `=== \"yes\"`."
msgstr "Отчетът пази настройките да / не като текст: `\"remote_login_enabled\": \"yes\"`, `\"remote_login_pwd_set\": \"no\"`. `if (doc.inventory.details.remote_login_pwd_set)` е true и за `\"no\"` - всеки непразен string е truthy. Сравнявайте със стойността, която имате предвид: `=== \"yes\"`."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:366
msgid "Truthy checks are good for one question: \"is there a value at all?\" `if (doc.overview)` means \"the document has an `overview` part\"."
msgstr "Truthy проверките са добри за един въпрос: \"има ли изобщо стойност?\" `if (doc.overview)` означава \"документът има част `overview`\"."

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:369
msgid "Comparing with `true` / `false`"
msgstr "Сравняване с `true` / `false`"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:371
msgid "Existing rules often contain lines like `if (present == false)` or `if (list.includes(x) !== true)` (`includes` on arrays comes in session 4). They work when the value is a real boolean, but `== false` converts: it also matches `0`, `\"\"` and even `\"0\"` - which is truthy!"
msgstr "В съществуващите правила често има редове като `if (present == false)` или `if (list.includes(x) !== true)` (`includes` за arrays идва в занятие 4). Те работят, когато стойността е истински boolean, но `== false` преобразува: съвпада и с `0`, `\"\"` и дори с `\"0\"` - който е truthy!"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:383
msgid "Write it shorter and safer:"
msgstr "Пишете го по-кратко и по-безопасно:"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:385
msgid "Instead of"
msgstr "Вместо"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:385
msgid "Write"
msgstr "Пишете"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:387
msgid "`if (!present)` or `if (present === false)`"
msgstr "`if (!present)` или `if (present === false)`"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:391
msgid "When you modernise a rule, check what the value can be. `!present` is also true for `null` and `undefined`, `present == false` is not. Usually `!present` is what the rule meant (\"not there or not set\"), but it is a change."
msgstr "Когато модернизирате правило, проверете какво може да бъде стойността. `!present` е true и за `null` и `undefined`, а `present == false` не е. Обикновено `!present` е това, което правилото е имало предвид (\"липсва или не е зададено\"), но все пак е промяна."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:396
msgid "**Types, comparisons and logic:** [5. Truthy and falsy](../animations/coercionAndLogic.html#5){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Типове, сравнения и логика:** [5. Truthy и falsy](../animations/coercionAndLogic.html#5){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 2
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:399
msgid "5. Short-circuit evaluation and defaults"
msgstr "5. Short-circuit изчисляване и стойности по подразбиране"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:401
msgid "`&&` and `||` stop as soon as the answer is known - this is called **short-circuit evaluation**. And they do not return `true` / `false`, but **one of the two operands**:"
msgstr "`&&` и `||` спират веднага щом отговорът е ясен - това се нарича **short-circuit evaluation**. И те не връщат `true` / `false`, а **единия от двата операнда**:"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:405
msgid "Expression"
msgstr "Израз"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:405
msgid "Returns"
msgstr "Връща"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:407
msgid "`a` if `a` is truthy, otherwise `b`"
msgstr "`a`, ако `a` е truthy, иначе `b`"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:408
msgid "`a` if `a` is falsy, otherwise `b`"
msgstr "`a`, ако `a` е falsy, иначе `b`"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:422
msgid "`||` for defaults"
msgstr "`||` за стойности по подразбиране"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:424
msgid "The sample rule uses `||` for a **fallback**: if the system name is missing or empty, use the device alias:"
msgstr "Примерното правило използва `||` за **fallback**: ако името на системата липсва или е празно, използва alias-а на устройството:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:436
msgid "Existing rules use it all the time:"
msgstr "Съществуващите правила го използват постоянно:"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:444
msgid "`&&` as a guard"
msgstr "`&&` като пазач (guard)"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:446
msgid "The right side runs **only** if the left side is truthy. Older rules use it to check every level of a path before reading the next one:"
msgstr "Дясната страна се изпълнява **само** ако лявата е truthy. По-старите правила го използват, за да проверят всяко ниво на един път, преди да прочетат следващото:"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:459
msgid "The trap: `||` replaces `0` and `\"\"` too"
msgstr "Капанът: `||` заменя и `0`, и `\"\"`"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:461
msgid "`||` replaces **every** falsy value. Sometimes `0`, `\"\"` or `false` is a real answer:"
msgstr "`||` заменя **всяка** falsy стойност. Понякога `0`, `\"\"` или `false` е истински отговор:"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:470
msgid "`??` - the nullish coalescing operator (ES2020)"
msgstr "`??` - nullish coalescing операторът (ES2020)"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:472
msgid "MDN: [Nullish coalescing operator (??)](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/Nullish_coalescing)"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:474
msgid "`a ?? b` returns `b` **only** when `a` is `null` or `undefined`:"
msgstr "`a ?? b` връща `b` **само** когато `a` е `null` или `undefined`:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:485
msgid "Use `??` when `0`, `\"\"` or `false` are valid values."
msgstr "Използвайте `??`, когато `0`, `\"\"` или `false` са валидни стойности."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:486
msgid "Use `||` when an empty value should also get the default."
msgstr "Използвайте `||`, когато и празна стойност трябва да получи стойността по подразбиране."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:489
msgid "`a || b ?? c` is a syntax error. Mixing `??` with `||` or `&&` needs parentheses: `(a || b) ?? c`."
msgstr "`a || b ?? c` е синтактична грешка. Смесването на `??` с `||` или `&&` изисква скоби: `(a || b) ?? c`."

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:493
msgid "Logical assignment (ES2021)"
msgstr "Логическо присвояване (ES2021)"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:495
msgid "MDN: [Logical OR assignment (||=)](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/Logical_OR_assignment), [Nullish coalescing assignment (??=)](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/Nullish_coalescing_assignment)"
msgstr ""

#. box title
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:507
msgid "ES2021+"
msgstr "ES2021+"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:508
msgid "Check that your rule engine supports `??=`, `||=` and `&&=` before you use them in a rule. `??` itself is ES2020, like `?.`."
msgstr "Проверете дали вашият rule engine поддържа `??=`, `||=` и `&&=`, преди да ги използвате в правило. Самият `??` е ES2020, като `?.`."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:513
msgid "**Types, comparisons and logic:** [6. Short-circuit: `&&` and `||`](../animations/coercionAndLogic.html#6){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Типове, сравнения и логика:** [6. Short-circuit: `&&` и `||`](../animations/coercionAndLogic.html#6){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 2
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:516
msgid "6. Conditional statements"
msgstr "6. Условни конструкции"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:518
msgid "MDN: [if...else](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Statements/if...else)"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:568
msgid "`x % 2` works, but `x % 2 !== 0` says what we mean. Prefer explicit conditions. (Not `x % 2 === 1`: for negative numbers `-3 % 2` is `-1`.)"
msgstr "`x % 2` работи, но `x % 2 !== 0` казва какво имаме предвид. Предпочитайте явни условия. (Не `x % 2 === 1`: за отрицателни числа `-3 % 2` е `-1`.)"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:583
msgid "It always starts with `if`."
msgstr "Винаги започва с `if`."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:584
msgid "Then zero or more `else if` blocks."
msgstr "След това нула или повече блока `else if`."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:585
msgid "`else` comes last. It is optional, but usually a good idea: it catches the case you did not think of."
msgstr "`else` е последен. Не е задължителен, но обикновено е добра идея: хваща случая, за който не сте се сетили."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:587
msgid "Only the **first** matching block runs."
msgstr "Изпълнява се само **първият** блок, чието условие е изпълнено."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:589
msgid "**Find the bug** - the code is valid JavaScript, but it gives wrong answers:"
msgstr "**Намерете бъга** - кодът е валиден JavaScript, но дава грешни отговори:"

#. box title
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:604 site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1092 site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1381
msgid "Answer"
msgstr "Отговор"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:605
msgid "The order. 25 is `> 12`, so the first block runs and `\"adult\"` is never reached. Check the **strictest** condition first: `age > 18`, then `age > 12`."
msgstr "Редът. 25 е `> 12`, затова се изпълнява първият блок и до `\"adult\"` никога не се стига. Проверявайте първо **най-строгото** условие: `age > 18`, после `age > 12`."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:609
msgid "The same matters for firmware levels. A level below the minimum is also below the recommended level, so the minimum is checked first:"
msgstr "Същото важи и за firmware levels. Ниво под минималното е и под препоръчителното, затова първо се проверява минималното:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:641
msgid "Change `current` to `\"4.2.0.5\"` and `\"4.10.0.0\"` and run again."
msgstr "Сменете `current` на `\"4.2.0.5\"` и на `\"4.10.0.0\"` и изпълнете отново."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:644
msgid "**Loops step by step:** [1. `if` / `else if`](../animations/loopsStepByStep.html#1){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Loops стъпка по стъпка:** [1. `if` / `else if`](../animations/loopsStepByStep.html#1){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:647
msgid "Two conditions, four answers"
msgstr "Две условия, четири отговора"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:649
msgid "A common case: two yes / no facts give four messages. Check \"both\" first:"
msgstr "Чест случай: два факта да / не дават четири съобщения. Проверете първо \"и двете\":"

#. box title
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:668
msgid "A missing key is not `\"\"`"
msgstr "Липсващ ключ не е `\"\"`"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:669
msgid "If the report has no `ntp_ip_address` key at all, the value is `undefined`, and `undefined !== \"\"` is `true` - the code above says \"reported\". Think about which values mean \"not reported\" (`undefined`, `null`, `\"\"`?) and check all of them. The homework asks exactly this."
msgstr "Ако в отчета изобщо няма ключ `ntp_ip_address`, стойността е `undefined`, а `undefined !== \"\"` е `true` - кодът по-горе казва \"reported\". Помислете кои стойности означават \"не е докладвано\" (`undefined`, `null`, `\"\"`?) и проверете всички. Домашното пита точно това."

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:675
msgid "Blocks and braces"
msgstr "Блокове и фигурни скоби"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:677
msgid "`{ }` groups statements into a **block**. With one statement the braces may be left out, and you will see that in rules:"
msgstr "`{ }` групира statements в **блок**. При един statement скобите могат да се пропуснат и ще го видите в правилата:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:685
msgid "That is fine for a short `return` on the same line. Everywhere else, write the braces - adding a second line later without them is a classic bug:"
msgstr "Това е добре за кратък `return` на същия ред. Навсякъде другаде пишете скобите - добавянето на втори ред по-късно без тях е класически бъг:"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:694
msgid "Guard clauses: stop early"
msgstr "Guard clauses: спрете рано"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:696
msgid "A rule does nothing for most documents. Instead of nesting `if` inside `if`, check what is **wrong** first and `return` (stop the rule) right away:"
msgstr "Едно правило не прави нищо за повечето документи. Вместо да влагате `if` в `if`, проверете първо какво **не е наред** и направете `return` (спрете правилото) веднага:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:721
msgid "`return` ends the function. Functions come in session 5 - for now, read `return` in a rule as \"stop here, no alert\"."
msgstr "`return` приключва функцията. Функциите идват в занятие 5 - засега четете `return` в правило като \"спри тук, без alert\"."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:748
msgid "MDN: [switch](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Statements/switch)"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:750
msgid "`switch` compares **one value** with several fixed values. It is an alternative to a long `if...else if` chain of `===` checks:"
msgstr "`switch` сравнява **една стойност** с няколко фиксирани стойности. Това е алтернатива на дълга верига `if...else if` от проверки с `===`:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:767
msgid "The value is compared with each `case` using `===` (strict)."
msgstr "Стойността се сравнява с всеки `case` чрез `===` (строго)."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:768
msgid "At a match, the code runs **until a `break`**."
msgstr "При съвпадение кодът се изпълнява **до `break`**."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:769
msgid "`default` runs when no `case` matches. Write it last."
msgstr "`default` се изпълнява, когато нито един `case` не съвпада. Пишете го последен."

#. box title
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:793
msgid "Forgotten `break`"
msgstr "Забравен `break`"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:794
msgid "Without `break`, the code \"falls through\" into the next case:"
msgstr "Без `break` кодът \"пропада\" в следващия case:"

#. box title
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:811
msgid "`switch` is strict"
msgstr "`switch` е строг"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:812
msgid "`switch (\"1\") { case 1: ... }` does **not** match: `\"1\" === 1` is false. Convert the JSON string first: `switch (Number(count))`."
msgstr "`switch (\"1\") { case 1: ... }` **не** съвпада: `\"1\" === 1` е false. Първо преобразувайте string-а от JSON: `switch (Number(count))`."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:817
msgid "**Loops step by step:** [7. `switch` without `break` (advanced)](../animations/loopsStepByStep.html#7){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Loops стъпка по стъпка:** [7. `switch` без `break` (advanced)](../animations/loopsStepByStep.html#7){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 2
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:820
msgid "8. The conditional (ternary) operator"
msgstr "8. Условният (тернарен) оператор"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:822
msgid "MDN: [Conditional (ternary) operator](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators/Conditional_operator)"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:828
msgid "The only operator with three operands. Unlike `if`, it **returns a value**, so it can be assigned, passed or put into a template string. These two are the same:"
msgstr "Единственият оператор с три операнда. За разлика от `if`, той **връща стойност**, затова може да се присвои, да се подаде или да се сложи в template string. Тези два варианта са еднакви:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:845
msgid "With the report:"
msgstr "С отчета:"

#. box title
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:856
msgid "One ternary is fine, two are too many"
msgstr "Един тернарен оператор е добре, два са твърде много"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:857
msgid "`a ? b : c ? d : e` is valid, but hard to read. Use `if...else if` instead."
msgstr "`a ? b : c ? d : e` е валидно, но трудно за четене. Вместо това използвайте `if...else if`."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:861
msgid "**Types, comparisons and logic:** [7. Ternary operator (advanced)](../animations/coercionAndLogic.html#7){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Типове, сравнения и логика:** [7. Тернарен оператор (advanced)](../animations/coercionAndLogic.html#7){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 2
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:864
msgid "9. Statements and expressions"
msgstr "9. Statements и expressions"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:866
msgid "MDN: [Statements and declarations](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Statements), [Expressions and operators](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Operators)"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:868
msgid "JavaScript code is made of two kinds of pieces:"
msgstr "Кодът на JavaScript се състои от два вида части:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:870
msgid "An **expression** produces a **value**. It can stand wherever a value is expected."
msgstr "**Expression** произвежда **стойност**. Може да стои навсякъде, където се очаква стойност."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:872
msgid "A **statement** **does** something, but has no value: declarations, `if`, `switch`, `return`, and the loops of the next section (`for`, `while`)."
msgstr "**Statement** **прави** нещо, но няма стойност: декларации, `if`, `switch`, `return` и loops от следващия раздел (`for`, `while`)."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:888
msgid "This is why the ternary works inside a template string and `if` does not:"
msgstr "Ето защо тернарният оператор работи в template string, а `if` - не:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:897
msgid "**How an expression is evaluated:** [6. Statement vs expression (advanced)](../animations/expressionEvaluation.html#6){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Как се изчислява един израз:** [6. Statement срещу expression (advanced)](../animations/expressionEvaluation.html#6){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 2
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:900
msgid "10. Loops"
msgstr "10. Loops"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:902
msgid "MDN: [Loops and iteration](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Guide/Loops_and_iteration), [for](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Statements/for), [while](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Statements/while)"
msgstr ""

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:904
msgid "A loop repeats a block of code. In rules you loop over the parts of a version, the characters of a string, and (from session 4) over lists of drives, nodes and records."
msgstr "Loop повтаря блок от код. В правилата обхождаме с loop частите на една версия, символите на един string и (от занятие 4) списъци от дискове, nodes и записи."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:916
msgid "The steps:"
msgstr "Стъпките:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:918
msgid "`init` runs **once**, first."
msgstr "`init` се изпълнява **веднъж**, най-напред."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:919
msgid "`condition` is checked: if true, the block runs; if false, the loop ends."
msgstr "Проверява се `condition`: ако е true, блокът се изпълнява; ако е false, loop-ът приключва."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:920
msgid "`update` runs after the block (usually `i++`)."
msgstr "`update` се изпълнява след блока (обикновено `i++`)."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:921
msgid "Back to step 2."
msgstr "Обратно към стъпка 2."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:929
msgid "The even numbers from 2 to 10:"
msgstr "Четните числа от 2 до 10:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:937
msgid "Building names of slots or drives:"
msgstr "Съставяне на имена на слотове или дискове:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:945
msgid "Counting down:"
msgstr "Обратно броене:"

#. box title
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:953
msgid "`var` in old rules"
msgstr "`var` в стари правила"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:954
msgid "Existing rules often write `for (var i = 0; ...)`. It works the same here, but `i` still exists after the loop. Write `let` in new code; the difference is explained in session 5."
msgstr "Съществуващите правила често пишат `for (var i = 0; ...)`. Тук работи по същия начин, но `i` продължава да съществува след loop-а. В нов код пишете `let`; разликата е обяснена в занятие 5."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:960
msgid "**Loops step by step:** [2. The `for` loop](../animations/loopsStepByStep.html#2){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Loops стъпка по стъпка:** [2. Loop-ът `for`](../animations/loopsStepByStep.html#2){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:963
msgid "Loops over a string"
msgstr "Loops върху string"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:965
msgid "A string has a **length** and each character has a **position** (index), starting from 0:"
msgstr "Един string има **дължина** (length) и всеки символ има **позиция** (индекс), като се брои от 0:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:980
msgid "Count the parts of a version (dots + 1):"
msgstr "Пребройте частите на една версия (точките + 1):"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:993
msgid "`for...of` (ES2015) gives the characters directly, when you do not need the index:"
msgstr "`for...of` (ES2015) дава директно символите, когато не ви трябва индексът:"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1005
msgid "Drawing a tree: nested loops"
msgstr "Рисуване на елха: вложени loops"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1007
msgid "A loop inside a loop. `\"*\".repeat(n)` gives `n` stars:"
msgstr "Loop в loop. `\"*\".repeat(n)` дава `n` звездички:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1037
msgid "The same with two real nested loops - each row builds its stars one by one:"
msgstr "Същото с два истински вложени loops - всеки ред съставя звездичките си една по една:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1050
msgid "**Loops step by step:** [6. Nested loops (advanced)](../animations/loopsStepByStep.html#6){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Loops стъпка по стъпка:** [6. Вложени loops (advanced)](../animations/loopsStepByStep.html#6){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1061
msgid "The condition is checked **before** each round. Something in the block must change it, otherwise the loop never ends:"
msgstr "Условието се проверява **преди** всеки кръг. Нещо в блока трябва да го промени, иначе loop-ът никога не свършва:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1072
msgid "This example is better as a `for` (see above): the number of rounds is known. Use `while` when you do **not** know in advance how many rounds are needed:"
msgstr "Този пример е по-добър като `for` (вижте по-горе): броят на кръговете е известен. Използвайте `while`, когато **не** знаете предварително колко кръга ще трябват:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1090
msgid "**Check yourself:** could you write the same logic with a `for` loop?"
msgstr "**Проверете се:** бихте ли написали същата логика с `for` loop?"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1093
msgid "Yes. The first guess goes into `init`, the new guess into `update`:"
msgstr "Да. Първото предположение отива в `init`, новото предположение - в `update`:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1103
msgid "Every `while` can be written as a `for` with empty `init` and `update`: `for (; condition; ) { ... }`. Choose the one that reads better - here `while`."
msgstr "Всеки `while` може да се напише като `for` с празни `init` и `update`: `for (; condition; ) { ... }`. Изберете този, който се чете по-добре - тук това е `while`."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1107
msgid "With the report - find all dots with `indexOf`, which returns the position of a text in a string, or `-1` if it is not there:"
msgstr "С отчета - намерете всички точки с `indexOf`, който връща позицията на текст в string или `-1`, ако текстът го няма:"

#. box title
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1123
msgid "`indexOf(...) !== -1` in old rules"
msgstr "`indexOf(...) !== -1` в стари правила"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1124
msgid "`platform.indexOf(\"virtual\") !== -1` means \"`platform` contains `virtual`\". The modern form is `platform.includes(\"virtual\")` (ES2015). And `model.indexOf(\"XR-\") === 0` means \"starts with\" - today `model.startsWith(\"XR-\")`."
msgstr "`platform.indexOf(\"virtual\") !== -1` означава \"`platform` съдържа `virtual`\". Модерната форма е `platform.includes(\"virtual\")` (ES2015). А `model.indexOf(\"XR-\") === 0` означава \"започва с\" - днес `model.startsWith(\"XR-\")`."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1131
msgid "**Loops step by step:** [3. `while` and the endless loop](../animations/loopsStepByStep.html#3){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Loops стъпка по стъпка:** [3. `while` и безкрайният loop](../animations/loopsStepByStep.html#3){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1136
msgid "Like `while`, but the condition is checked **after** the block - so the block runs **at least once**:"
msgstr "Като `while`, но условието се проверява **след** блока - затова блокът се изпълнява **поне веднъж**:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1156
msgid "`do...while` is rare in rules; recognise it when you see it."
msgstr "`do...while` се среща рядко в правилата; разпознавайте го, когато го видите."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1159
msgid "**Loops step by step:** [4. `do...while`](../animations/loopsStepByStep.html#4){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Loops стъпка по стъпка:** [4. `do...while`](../animations/loopsStepByStep.html#4){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 3
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1162
msgid "`break` and `continue`"
msgstr "`break` и `continue`"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1164
msgid "`break` - leave the loop **now**."
msgstr "`break` - излез от loop-а **веднага**."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1165
msgid "`continue` - skip the rest of **this round**, go to the next one."
msgstr "`continue` - прескочи останалата част от **този кръг** и мини към следващия."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1167
msgid "Cut the version out of the firmware level - stop at the first space:"
msgstr "Изрежете версията от firmware level - спрете при първия интервал:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1183
msgid "Keep only digits and dots - skip everything else:"
msgstr "Запазете само цифрите и точките - прескочете всичко останало:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1199
msgid "The output shows that cleaning data needs care: skipping `-` glued two parts together. In session 8 we do this properly with regular expressions."
msgstr "Резултатът показва, че почистването на данни иска внимание: прескачането на `-` слепи две части. В занятие 8 ще направим това както трябва, с regular expressions."

#. box title
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1202
msgid "Endless loops"
msgstr "Безкрайни loops"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1203
msgid "If the condition never becomes false, the page or the rule hangs. In the browser, close the tab; in the terminal, press `Ctrl+C`. Before you run a `while`, ask: what changes the condition?"
msgstr "Ако условието никога не стане false, страницата или правилото увисва. В браузъра затворете таба; в терминала натиснете `Ctrl+C`. Преди да пуснете `while`, запитайте се: какво променя условието?"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1209
msgid "**Loops step by step:** [5. `break` and `continue`](../animations/loopsStepByStep.html#5){target=\"_blank\"}"
msgstr "**Loops стъпка по стъпка:** [5. `break` и `continue`](../animations/loopsStepByStep.html#5){target=\"_blank\"}"

#. heading 2
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1212
msgid "11. Reading existing rules"
msgstr "11. Четене на съществуващи правила"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1214
msgid "First, run the rule from the start of the lecture. `emit` is a fake here: it only prints the alert."
msgstr "Първо изпълнете правилото от началото на лекцията. Тук `emit` е фалшива: само извежда alert-а."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1290
msgid "Change the firmware level of the older device to `\"4.2.0.5 (build 420.5)\"`, then to `\"\"`, and run again. Which lines decide the result each time?"
msgstr "Сменете firmware level на по-старото устройство на `\"4.2.0.5 (build 420.5)\"`, после на `\"\"`, и изпълнете отново. Кои редове решават резултата всеки път?"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1293
msgid "Many existing rules are written in an older style (before ES2015). Here is **the same rule** in that style - you need to read it with ease, and decide when to modernise it:"
msgstr "Много съществуващи правила са написани в по-стар стил (преди ES2015). Ето **същото правило** в този стил - трябва да можете да го четете с лекота и да решите кога да го модернизирате:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1367
msgid "**Check yourself:**"
msgstr "**Проверете се:**"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1369
msgid "List the differences you see between the two versions. Which ones change only the style, and which could change the result?"
msgstr "Избройте разликите, които виждате между двете версии. Кои променят само стила и кои биха могли да променят резултата?"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1371
msgid "What does `info && info.json && info.json.data && info.json.data.system && info.json.data.system.name || doc.status.device_alias` return when `extended_info` is `{}`? And when `extended_info` is missing?"
msgstr "Какво връща `info && info.json && info.json.data && info.json.data.system && info.json.data.system.name || doc.status.device_alias`, когато `extended_info` е `{}`? А когато `extended_info` липсва?"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1373
msgid "The two rules are **not** exactly the same. Look at the model in the second call: `\"xr-210\"`, in lower case. Which rule creates an alert for it, and why? Run the modern rule with that document to check."
msgstr "Двете правила **не** са напълно еднакви. Вижте модела във второто извикване: `\"xr-210\"`, с малки букви. Кое правило създава alert за него и защо? Изпълнете модерното правило с този документ, за да проверите."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1376
msgid "The old rule uses `|| \"\"` for `level`, the new one `?? \"\"`. Can that make a difference here?"
msgstr "Старото правило използва `|| \"\"` за `level`, новото - `?? \"\"`. Може ли това да промени нещо тук?"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1378
msgid "Both rules start with a guard clause. Is it enough? Find a small document that makes **both** rules stop with an error. How would you fix the guard?"
msgstr "И двете правила започват с guard clause. Достатъчна ли е? Намерете малък документ, при който **и двете** правила спират с грешка. Как бихте поправили guard clause-а?"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1382
msgid "Style only: `var` -> `const` / `let`; `==` / `!=` -> `===` / `!==` (here both sides are strings, so the result is the same); `charAt(i)` -> `for...of`; `== true` -> nothing; `new Object()` + `details[\"...\"] = ...` -> an object literal; a ternary instead of the `switch`; the `&&` chain -> `?.`. Could change the result: `String(...)` and `.toUpperCase()` around the model (question 3), and `||` vs `??` (question 4)."
msgstr "Само стил: `var` -> `const` / `let`; `==` / `!=` -> `===` / `!==` (тук и двете страни са strings, затова резултатът е същият); `charAt(i)` -> `for...of`; `== true` -> нищо; `new Object()` + `details[\"...\"] = ...` -> обектен литерал; тернарен оператор вместо `switch`; веригата с `&&` -> `?.`. Могат да променят резултата: `String(...)` и `.toUpperCase()` около модела (въпрос 3) и `||` срещу `??` (въпрос 4)."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1388
msgid "`doc.status.device_alias` in both cases: `info.json` is `undefined` (falsy), so the `&&` chain stops and returns `undefined`, and `||` takes the alias. When `extended_info` is missing, `info` itself is `undefined` - same result. Note: `&&` is evaluated before `||`."
msgstr "`doc.status.device_alias` и в двата случая: `info.json` е `undefined` (falsy), затова веригата с `&&` спира и връща `undefined`, а `||` взема alias-а. Когато `extended_info` липсва, самото `info` е `undefined` - същият резултат. Обърнете внимание: `&&` се изчислява преди `||`."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1392
msgid "Only the old one: it upper-cases the model first, so `\"xr-210\"` becomes `\"XR-210\"`. The modern rule compares the model as it is and stops. Whether that is a bug or a feature depends on the data - if the JSON can contain lower-case models, the modern rule should normalise too."
msgstr "Само старото: то първо прави модела с главни букви, затова `\"xr-210\"` става `\"XR-210\"`. Модерното правило сравнява модела както е и спира. Дали това е бъг или полезно поведение, зависи от данните - ако JSON може да съдържа модели с малки букви, модерното правило също трябва да нормализира."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1396
msgid "Not for strings: `\"\" || \"\"` and `\"\" ?? \"\"` are both `\"\"`. It matters only if `firmware_level` were not a string - for example the number `0`: the old rule turns it into `\"\"` and stops; the new one keeps `0`, and `for...of` over a number is an error. The old `String(...)` is a good habit: convert first, then loop."
msgstr "Не и за strings: `\"\" || \"\"` и `\"\" ?? \"\"` са `\"\"` и двете. Има значение само ако `firmware_level` не е string - например number `0`: старото правило го превръща в `\"\"` и спира; новото запазва `0`, а `for...of` върху number е грешка. Старото `String(...)` е добър навик: първо преобразувайте, после обхождайте."

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1401
msgid "No. The guard checks `overview` and `inventory`, but the rules also read `doc.inventory.details` and (when there is no system name) `doc.status`. For example `{ overview: { model: \"XR-210\" }, inventory: {}, status: { device_alias: \"X\" } }` passes the guard, and then `doc.inventory.details.firmware_level` is an error: `details` is `undefined`. Fix: check every part you read without `?.`: `if (!doc.overview || !doc.inventory || !doc.inventory.details || !doc.status) return;` (or, in the modern style, `if (!doc.overview || !doc.inventory?.details || !doc.status) return;`)."
msgstr "Не. Guard clause-ът проверява `overview` и `inventory`, но правилата четат също `doc.inventory.details` и (когато няма име на системата) `doc.status`. Например `{ overview: { model: \"XR-210\" }, inventory: {}, status: { device_alias: \"X\" } }` минава през guard clause-а и след това `doc.inventory.details.firmware_level` е грешка: `details` е `undefined`. Поправка: проверете всяка част, която четете без `?.`: `if (!doc.overview || !doc.inventory || !doc.inventory.details || !doc.status) return;` (или в модерния стил `if (!doc.overview || !doc.inventory?.details || !doc.status) return;`)."

#. heading 2
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1411
msgid "12. Practice"
msgstr "12. Упражнения"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1413
msgid "In your copy of the Homework repository, first get the new tasks:"
msgstr "Във вашето копие на Homework repository първо вземете новите задачи:"

#. paragraph
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1420
msgid "Each file explains the task at the top. Write your code between the `your code` lines; the checks at the bottom print `OK` or `FAIL`."
msgstr "Всеки файл обяснява задачата в началото си. Пишете кода си между редовете `your code`; проверките най-долу извеждат `OK` или `FAIL`."

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1423
msgid "Task"
msgstr "Задача"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1423
msgid "File"
msgstr "Файл"

#. table cell
#: site/lectures/03-conditions-and-loops.md:1423
msgid "What you do"
msgstr "Какво правите"

